  "title": "ticfac-exec-subprocess start has no --try flag",
  "body": "The manual executor CLI accepts --attempt but not --try, so a hand-started attempt's runner sees TICFAC_TRY=0 rather than the tick's real try count. Nothing keys on it today; a --try flag (defaulting alongside --attempt) would keep the manual surface honest with the env contract the reconciler's dispatches now speak.",
